+# Woodward note candidate in Commission archive mirror
+
+**TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1.** A previously indexed six-page PDF titled `T7 B13 Woodward Notes Fdr- Michael Woodward Note and Note from same fax 731.pdf` was acquired on 2026-11-15 from the [public 2009 Commission-records ZIP mirror](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip). Its ZIP member name, offset, compression, byte count, CRC-32 and SHA-256 were checked; SHA-256 is `47ad462b2895fde090c8b2ef1271f9b1d6a16920c76b4420290ce2dfa63ad3a3`. The exact archive member and byte-range provenance are in SOURCE-PINS.json. An unaffiliated public [reader](https://www.scribd.com/document/19131561/T7-B13-Woodward-Notes-Fdr-Michael-Woodward-Note-and-Note-From-Same-Fax-731) labels a six-page document similarly; reader content was not used to authenticate the downloaded bytes.
+
+**Observations.** The acquired PDF's physical p. 1 labels material as Woodward notes. Physical pp. 2–3 show a handwritten note about Sweeney; p. 2 has an apparent signature and a handwritten `9-11-01` date. The copied pages also carry later fax markings, including 2004 dates. These visible marks are different fields and do not prove when the handwriting was made or received. The reviewed handwritten content on pp. 2–3 does not visibly specify whether the call used an onboard phone or a personal cell phone; this is a limited reading of those pages, not proof that no other record identifies the device. Some handwriting is difficult to read. Physical pp. 4–6 were not inspected; the document is not represented as fully read.
+
+**Relationship to earlier records.** The [previously reviewed FBI interview reproduction](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report/9-11-interviews-2001-09-sep-02-of-08/at_download/file#page=25) reports that Woodward signed, dated and provided notes to an agent. The acquired archive copy is a plausible candidate for comparison, but its custody chain, handwriting, the relationship to the agent's received set, and completeness are not authenticated. Its note page's lack of an explicit service label does not independently resolve the previously preserved differing interview and later reconstruction descriptions of Sweeney's device. Do not treat versions of one note as independent witnesses or infer fabrication from this uncertainty. [Earlier review and open conflicts](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/tree/main/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-operator-continuations-2026-10-31).
+
